Data Dictionary - Obesity Dataset

Gender_Male is 1 if the respondent is male and 0 if female.
Age is the respondent’s age in years.
Family_History_of_Overweight is 1 if the respondent has a family member who is or has been overweight, 0 if not.
High-Calorie_Consumption_Frequency is 1 if the respondent frequently consumes high-calorie foods, 0 if not.
Frequent_Vegetable_Consumption is 1 if the respondent usually eats vegetables with meals, 0 if not.
Meals_Per_Day represents how many main meals the respondent eats daily (0 for 1–2 meals, 1 for 3 meals, and 2 for more than 3 meals).
Snacking represents how much food the respondent consumes between meals on a scale of 0 to 3.
Water_Intake represents how much fluid the respondent consumes on a scale of 0 to 2.
Calorie_Intake_Tracking is 1 if the respondent tracks their calorie intake, 0 if not.
Physical_Activity_Level represents how much physical activity the respondent engages in on a scale of 0 to 3.
Screen_Time represents how much time the respondent spends looking at screen-based devices on a scale of 0 to 2.
Alcohol_Consumption represents how often the respondent consumes alcohol on a scale of 0 to 3.
Car_Transportation indicates that the primary mode of transportation is a car.
Bicycle_Transportation indicates that the primary mode of transportation is a bicycle
Motorcycle_Transportation indicates that the primary mode of transportation is a motorcycle
Public_Transport indicates that the primary mode of transportation is public transportation (Bus, Train, Subway)
Walking_Transport indicates that the primary mode of transportation is Walking
Obese is 1 if the patient is obese and 0 if not.
Smoker is 1 if the respondent smokes, 0 if not.
